      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Switching to hardware security keys primarily closes critical vulnerabilities associated with SIM-swapping attacks and SMS delivery failures, which hardware keys do not support. Unlike SMS, which relies on public mobile networks vulnerable to interception and social engineering, FIDO2 keys use cryptographic signatures that are immune to these foreseeable threats. By adopting this standard, your firm directly mitigates the risk of credential stuffing and unauthorized account takeovers that often exploit weak or intercepted second-factor authentication channels.",
      "source": "target",
